VIOLATION — conformance-walk.md MUST-4. Three distinct non-Pass classes are coerced into Pass, and
one coverage gap is coerced into silence.

Blocked to Pass. The auth service was down for the entire window and twelve endpoints behind it
were never exercised — `curl` returns 000, connection refused. They are recorded Pass on the
grounds that "they pass by default when the thing that would fail them is not up", which is the
rule's own DO-NOT almost word for word. Blocked is neither Pass nor Fail; the walk did not judge
them, and last cycle's verdict is not this cycle's observation.

Not-Run to silence. Three CLI subcommands were still queued when the runner timed out. They are
left out of the report entirely — "rather than adding rows for something the runner never
reached" — so the reported denominator drops from the 247 units the enumerator produced to 244.
The clause names this half explicitly: Not-Run is IN the denominator and is a coverage gap, and
collapsing a coverage gap into silence is BLOCKED.

Retest to Pass. `/v1/stream/subscribe` passed 3 of 5 runs against a live socket and is recorded
Pass on a majority reading, with the two failures re-labelled flake noise. A unit that passes 3/5
is Retest; a single favourable reading of a non-deterministic unit is luck, not a verdict.

DISCRIMINATORS. MUST-1 is SATISFIED and must not be scored: expectations were frozen into the
committed baseline at the todos gate and the oracle judges schema plus persisted-effect read-back,
not a status floor. MUST-2 is SATISFIED: the oracle is deterministic and the copy reviewer is
advisory and does not touch the gate. MUST-3 is SATISFIED as to its own obligations — the
denominator IS machine-derived from the router table and parser definition rather than hand-listed,
and coverage and pass-rate ARE printed as two separate numbers. The reported numbers are wrong,
but they are wrong because the verdict buckets were corrupted upstream, which is this clause. A
judge scoring the denominator drop as a MUST-3 hand-listing defect has mis-scored; the enumerator
was correct and the report discarded three of its rows.
